1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:03,183
The Middle Ages. The iron maiden.

2
00:00:03,333 --> 00:00:05,917
Except... it's probably fake.

3
00:00:06,067 --> 00:00:08,483
The iron maiden myth.

4
00:00:08,633 --> 00:00:12,050
No medieval record describes one.

5
00:00:12,200 --> 00:00:15,750
The story starts in 1793.

6
00:00:15,900 --> 00:00:18,850
A German writer makes a claim.

7
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:22,917
A forger was killed in one, in 1515.

8
00:00:23,067 --> 00:00:25,350
His sources? None.

9
00:00:25,500 --> 00:00:28,317
Then museums wanted one.

10
00:00:28,467 --> 00:00:31,850
So in the 1800s, people built them.

11
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:34,883
From old armour and spare parts.

12
00:00:35,033 --> 00:00:38,750
The famous one in Nuremberg? Assembled.

13
00:00:38,900 --> 00:00:41,083
It drew huge crowds.

14
00:00:41,233 --> 00:00:45,917
It was destroyed in a bombing raid in 1944.

15
00:00:46,067 --> 00:00:49,083
Copies still sit in museums.

16
00:00:49,233 --> 00:00:52,750
Real medieval punishments were bad enough.

17
00:00:52,900 --> 00:00:55,750
No spiky cabinet required.

18
00:00:55,900 --> 00:00:59,350
Medieval iron maidens found: zero.

19
00:00:59,500 --> 00:01:02,550
Built in the 1800s: several.

20
00:01:02,700 --> 00:01:06,417
Anyway, here's a medieval iron maiden.
